# Secret-reference login in guided runs — technical design

Status: **R3 — canonical design for secret-reference login on the single observed path ([ADR-SC-005](../../architecture/ADR-SC-005-single-path-observed-authoring.md)).** Written by Aria (@architect), 2026-10-09; R3 the same day after the user accepted the single-path ruling. Design only: no code, schema, migration, OpenAPI, test or story file is changed by this document. Every `path:line` below was read on this working tree on 2026-10-09 (HEAD `d954a21c5`); line numbers drift. R3 removes every legacy-compile-path variant (the compile path is retired by STUDIO-OBS-012A): the password-only rule has one adapter and no opt-out; `LOGIN_REQUIRED` is computed from the observation signature on both guided learn and observed replay; migrations follow the ADR-SC-005 D-B re-baseline (V34 absorbed); the backend→runner hop is one TLS/client-certificate hop to one runner process; §10 maps items onto the ADR-SC-005 story set. Incremental re-learn (ADR-SC-005 D-D) does not change this design: a `secretRef` fill in a reused prefix step is replayed by the observed adapter under the same rules.

## 0. Decision record

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Date | 2026-10-09 |
| Decider | User / product owner |
| Decision | In Studio observed/guided authoring, login is **owned by the test author**, exactly as it was in the retired compile flow. If a step uses a login-protected page, the author writes login steps before it and references credentials as `<secret ID>` exactly the way nonsecret values use `<var NAME>`. There is **no** external account/session provider, **no** same-session sign-in handoff, **no** account-selection UI. EXT-001 is dropped. |
| Supersedes | [account-provider-readiness-design.md](account-provider-readiness-design.md) R1–R3 in full (historical); [consensus-plan.md](consensus-plan.md) §8 first two paragraphs and §9 "Authentication needed" row (amended in place); OBS-007 Draft tasks D0–D4/D6; GA plan §6 "ARCH-10 … ports dropped by the decision" is confirmed. |
| Not reopened | Account providers, handoff, cookie import, account-selection UI, "Sign in securely". |
| R3 delta (2026-10-09) | Single path per [ADR-SC-005](../../architecture/ADR-SC-005-single-path-observed-authoring.md): legacy variants removed from §§1–7; §4.2 limit restated (multi-password pages and non-password targets unsupported at GA, no fallback adapter); §5 replay annotation via the observed adapter's observation; §6 migrations re-baselined (V34 absorbed into V14/V15/V16/V17); I-C8/Q4 one runner process with runner-terminated TLS + client certificate; §8 Q1 and Q4 decided; §10 remapped to STUDIO-OBS-007/012A/012B/013/014/015/008/009/010/011. Security review R2 verdict unchanged; a delta check of R3 by @qa (security) is owed before OBS-007 develop. |
| Security inputs adopted | SEC requirements 1–10 of the 2026-10-09 security review, with one recorded deviation (§4, password-only rule without opt-out — the only rule on the single path, R3) and one placement note (§6, ARCH-9). |
| Security review of this design | 2026-10-09 **PASS-WITH-CONDITIONS** ([secret-login-security-review.md](secret-login-security-review.md)). Revision R1 of this document adopts F-1…F-10: trusted password-field resolution at fill time (F-1, §4.2), honest post-release window plus `revoked` control (F-2, I-A3), browser-profile sink (F-3), read/write String residuals (F-4), single 4096 bound (F-5), password-control read refusal (F-6), runner digest excludes `secret` (F-7), `RunnerReport.secretUse` contract bump (F-8), gate G-3 (F-9), capacity/raw-error/manual-video oracles (F-10). **R2** (same day) folds the R1 delta check: F-1…F-10 closed, verdict unchanged; R1-1 element-identity continuity under the collector's `acquire` guard, R1-2 form-action origin refusal and whole-origin trust statement, R1-3 single visibility/candidate function (§4.2, §4.3, I-A1, C-18…C-20). |

## 1. Verified starting point (what the code does today)

| Fact | Evidence |
|---|---|
| Guided input kinds are `nonsecretText \| destination` only; a value is required on both | `studio-runner/src/guided/types.ts:6`; `contracts/v2/authored-inputs.schema.json` (both variants require `value`) |
| Classifier already parses `<secret ID>`, requires it declared (`FORBIDDEN_SCOPE`), but emits configuration references only for `var` names; a secret can never reach a fill | `GuidedSourceClassifier.java:19,60-77,107-124,152-171` (`used.add(name)` only for `var`) |
| Every guided start fails `AUTH_CONNECTION_REQUIRED` | `GuidedSessionService.java:319-323`; `GuidedSessionConfiguration.java:99-113` |
| `knownSecrets` is always `[]`; collector merges/withholds and wipes on dispose; sanitizer bound 64×4096 | `guided/runtime.ts:77`; `run/observedReplayAdapter.ts:17`; `run/browser.ts:335-336,452`; `observationCollector.ts:60`; `observationSanitizer.ts:19` |
| The trusted collector **never emits a password control as a node**: `type=password` ⇒ `hard` ⇒ `!eligibleSource` ⇒ `blocked` ⇒ `!safe` ⇒ only `coverage.withheldRegions++`; a node whose name/placeholder/testid matches `/password|passcode|secret|credential|…/` is withheld too. The model has no node to target; §5 cannot read `controlType` from nodes (security review F-1, confirmed) | `observationCollector.ts:62,98,103,301,391,395-396` |
| The ordinary dispatch pass (shared by observed replay) resolves secrets at dispatch only, erases on every exit path, carries `secretOrigins`, refuses fill off-origin, records vault versions; the `playwrightAdapter.ts` origin check cited here leaves with the compile path (OBS-012A) and is re-implemented in the observed adapter (§4.3) | `VaultStudioReferenceResolver.java:63-137`; `StudioReferenceResolver.java` (`Resolved` is `AutoCloseable`); `StudioDispatcher.java:320-322,501-506`; `run/protocol.ts:106-113`; `run/playwrightAdapter.ts:504-520` (`requireSecretOrigin`) |
| No login detection exists on any path today (guided runs end in a validator rejection or `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`; replay ends `TARGET_DRIFT`) | `run/errors.ts`, `executor/observedReplay.ts`, `guided/translation/GuidedTranslationService.java` (grep for login: none) |
| Observed replay job carries `accountHandle` and derives `scope` from it; `installCookies`/`enter` exist on the recorded context | `ObservedReplayAuthorization.java:326-345`; `run/childRuntime.ts:853-875`; `run/browser.ts:181-193`; `contracts/v2/replay-job.schema.json` (`accountHandle` required) |
| Account artifacts in DB check functions: `scope.accountRef`, binding `accountAuthorization`, grant/receipt `accountGrantId`, profile `accountAbi:1` | `V33__studio_observed_publication.sql:300,310-311,346,366-379,391-396`; `V30:13-14` state CHECK includes `AWAITING_AUTH` |
| No production guided data exists: publication and observed replay default off, guided worker has no `CMD`/chart | `application.yml:203-215`; `studio-runner/Dockerfile` (only `dist/main.js`); `run/guidedMain.ts` needs `STUDIO_GUIDED_CONFIG_FILE` |

Contradictions with the brief are listed in §9.

## 2. Target flow (one page)

```
author: "Enter <var USER> as username" / "Enter <secret PASS> as password" / "Click Sign in" / "Open reports" / …
  classify  → sourceReference{kind:secretRef, intendedSlot:fill.value, referenceName:PASS}; preflight(mayUse + exists), no read
  plan      → model sees step text with the token span masked, the reference (ID), never a value
  materialize → authoredInputs += {kind:secretRef, secretId:PASS}  (no value; hashed into authoredInputsHash)
  propose   → fill.value = {kind:secretRef, sourceInputId}, target = {kind:passwordControl, documentId, generation}  (node-free: the collector never exports a password node)
  prepare   → mayUse recheck (names only); trusted runner proves exactly one visible enabled input[type=password] in the current top-level document
  dispatch  → backend resolve() from Vault (CSI/env/testId/principal scope), RELEASE audit row, send BridgeDispatch.secret on mTLS bridge, erase
  act       → trusted runner re-resolves that unique password input at fill time (0 or >1 ⇒ POLICY_DENIED), origin ∈ allowedOrigins ∩ approvedOrigins, withhold(value) BEFORE fill, fill via the pinned handle
  observe   → next observation is the reached document; knownSecrets scrubs any echo
  publish   → artifact fill value {kind:secretRef, sourceInputId}; inputRecipes {kind:secretRef, referenceName:PASS}; no value anywhere
  replay    → job.secrets/secretOrigins resolved per run by the ordinary dispatch pass, same origin + password rule in the observed adapter, model-free
  stop      → knownSecrets = [], inventory disposed, dispatch frame not retained
```

## 3. Data model and contracts (closed shapes, v3)

**Why a new directory, not in-place edits.** `contracts/v2/` is the frozen OBS-004..006 review basis (closure digests cite it). Create `contracts/v3/` by copy-and-edit; `tools/build-studio-observed-schemas.cjs` regenerates `studio-runner/src/guided/{schemas.json,types.ts}`, `validator/observedSchemas.json`, `executor/observedOperations.ts`, backend `studio/observed-contracts/v3`. v1 and v2 stay on disk until OBS-011 (ARCH-10) retires v1 and marks v2 historical.

